# fpl-x project context

Personal CLI: fetch **Bruno Mars XI** (manager `4703066`), render a pitch PNG, optionally post to X. Full agent brief: `AGENTS.md`. Graphic/caption work: `.cursor/skills/fpl-team-graphic/SKILL.md`.

## Run (Git Bash)

```bash
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m fpl_x publish --dry-run
```

Use that interpreter with forward slashes. Default to dry-run. Do not tweet unless the user asks.

## Code map

- `src/fpl_x/cli.py` — `publish`
- `src/fpl_x/fpl.py` — fetch + `TeamSnapshot.caption()`
- `src/fpl_x/render.py` — Playwright PNG
- `src/fpl_x/twitter.py` — OAuth 1.0a post
- `src/fpl_x/templates/team_card.html` — visual source of truth
- Preview: `output/gw{N}.png`

## Must not

- Commit or paste `.env` / `FPL_ACCESS_TOKEN` / X keys
- Put URLs on the graphic or in the caption
- Change caption shape without updating `TeamSnapshot.caption()`
- Treat this as a multi-user product; keep diffs small
